  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certifies that on 29th August 2006, an erection of a single storey rear extension, giving a total volume increase to the original house of 35.96m3, as shown on drawing numbers P06-38, received 29 August 2006, was unlawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nFollowing the proposed erection of a single storey rear extension, the resulting building would fall outside the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995, as the development is not located entirely within the curtilage of the dwellinghouse. Full Planning permission will therefore be required.\r\n"
